                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237494495",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199369638487",
                            "num_reviews": 360,
                            "playtime_forever": 76,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 76,
                            "deck_playtime_at_review": 76,
                            "last_played": 1790911038
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "To this very day, occasionally I still go back to P.T (aka SHPT), playing Silent Hills with the corridors loop. Already beat it and still returning. Because the lore was... and still great!\nEven as just a piece of demo / playable teaser. \n\nImagine if we get the whole complete game, that will be awesome!\n\nThis one; Silent Descent, is taking the style of SHPT. \nIt's not that good, but not quite bad either. The puzzles, jumpscares, plot and reality bending are simply good enough and will mistakenly think that you're playing the next level of SHPT, though it was not intended to be. \nBecause this is a different game yet using the same formula as SHPT.\nSo if you like SHPT, please give this one a try.\n\nYet I still yearning and couldn't move on from SHPT.\nSilent Hills Playable Teaser (SHPT) was a dream team project. \nIt was planned as a collaboration between game director Hideo Kojima, filmmaker Guillermo del Toro, and horror manga legend Junji Ito, starring actor Norman Reedus. Too bad it never gonna happened. \n\nQuite devastating that it will never come to light.\n\nThough I am still hoping it will be.\n\nSomeday, somehow.\n",
